/*  FUNCTION NAME:      TOPOS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Converts anything to a scalar packed position: A1-style address text encodes as an absolute position (ROW * _mult + COLUMN), any direction spelling (via DIRDELTA) becomes a relative movement delta, and numbers pass through unchanged.*/
/*  RETURNS:            integer position (row*_mult+col) for an address, packed delta for a direction; lifts
    PARAMETERS:
        value           (Required) A cell address as text (e.g. "E5"; any number of column letters, so "XFE1" and "ABCD9" work, and rows past 1048576; sheet prefixes and $ anchors are ignored; for a range such as "B2:D9" only the first cell, B2, is used), OR a direction in any spelling DIRDELTA accepts (arrow glyph ↑ ↗ → ↘ ↓ ↙ ← ↖, compass code N, NE, North-East ..., screen direction U, DR, up-left ...), OR a number (passes through unchanged, so pre-packed positions, deltas and knight moves survive). Also accepts an array/range of values - result lifts element-wise. Text that is not an address or a direction returns a message "TOPOS: can't read ..." (text, so it shows in the cell; arithmetic on it gives #VALUE!).
        mult            (Optional) Multiplier for the row component. Default: the _mult constant (1000000), which fits any column up to 999999 (ZZZZ = 475254) and keeps the trailing 6 digits readable as the column. A column >= mult returns a message rather than a wrong number. Applies to both branches: addresses encode as ROW*mult+COLUMN, direction deltas repack as rowDelta*mult+colDelta.
    EXAMPLE:            =TOPOS("E5") -> 5000005 (and =TOPOS("↑") returns -1000000)
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-04-15  Claude      Initial version (as CELLTOPOS)
                        2026-05-14  Claude      Switch to string input; parse address directly (non-volatile, no INDIRECT)
                        2026-05-14  Claude      Default mult bumped from 1000 to 100000 — safe for any Excel column (max XFD=16384) while keeping the trailing 5 digits readable
                        2026-05-14  Claude      Array-lift via dispatcher: MAP over multi-cell input, otherwise scalar body unchanged
                        2026-07-22  Claude      Deref the scalar branch with @: 1x1 arrays previously reached the scalar body array-shaped, where SEQUENCE(LEN) lifts element-wise and truncates multi-letter columns ("BY85" parsed as AZ85). Unconditional MAP is NOT the fix - MAP returns a 1x1 array even for scalar input, re-poisoning downstream SEQUENCE consumers (MAZE path mode) (#318)
                        2026-08-28  Claude      Generalised and renamed CELLTOPOS -> TOPOS: non-address text routes through DIRDELTA to a relative packed delta (repacked for custom mult); numbers pass through unchanged
                        2026-11-06  Claude      Default mult is now the _mult constant (1000000); any number of column letters and rows past 1048576; unparseable text returns a readable "TOPOS: ..." message instead of a silent #N/A; a column that does not fit under mult is reported, not mis-packed (#380)
*/
TOPOS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [value],
    [mult],
    LET(
    //  Check inputs
        Help?, ISOMITTED(value),
    //  Procedure
        m, IF(ISOMITTED(mult), _mult, mult),
        scalar, LAMBDA(v,
                  IF(ISNUMBER(v), v,
                    LET(
                      afterSheet, IFERROR(TEXTAFTER(v, "!", -1), v),
                      firstCell, IFERROR(TEXTBEFORE(afterSheet, ":"), afterSheet),
                      upper, SUBSTITUTE(UPPER(firstCell), "$", ""),
                      IF(REGEXTEST(upper, "^[A-Z]+0*[1-9][0-9]*$"),
                        LET(
                          letters, REGEXEXTRACT(upper, "[A-Z]+"),
                          rowNum, --REGEXEXTRACT(upper, "\d+"),
                          n, LEN(letters),
                          colNum, SUMPRODUCT((CODE(MID(letters, SEQUENCE(n), 1)) - 64) * 26^(n - SEQUENCE(n))),
                          IF(colNum < m, rowNum * m + colNum,
                             "TOPOS: column " & letters & " (" & colNum & ") does not fit under mult " & m)),
                        LET(
                          delta, DIRDELTA(v),
                          rowDelta, ROUND(delta / _mult, 0),
                          colDelta, delta - rowDelta * _mult,
                          IF(ISERROR(delta),
                             "TOPOS: can't read '" & v & "' (not an address, direction or number)",
                             rowDelta * m + colDelta)))))),
        result, IF(OR(ROWS(value) > 1, COLUMNS(value) > 1),
                    MAP(value, scalar),
                    scalar(@value)),
    //  Help
        IF(Help?, TEXTSPLIT(
                "FUNCTION:      ¦TOPOS(value, [mult])¶" &
                "DESCRIPTION:   ¦Converts anything to a scalar packed position: A1-style address text encodes as an absolute position ROW*mult+COLUMN, any direction spelling becomes a relative movement delta (via DIRDELTA), and numbers pass through unchanged.¶" &
                "VERSION:       ¦Nov 06 2026¶" &
                "PARAMETERS:    ¦¶" &
                "   value          ¦(Required) A cell address as text (e.g. ""E5""; any number of column letters, so ""XFE1"" and ""ABCD9"" work, and rows past 1048576; sheet prefixes and $ anchors are ignored; for a range such as ""B2:D9"" only the first cell, B2, is used), OR a direction in any spelling DIRDELTA accepts (arrow glyph ↑ ↗ → ↘ ↓ ↙ ← ↖, compass code N, NE, North-East ..., screen direction U, DR, up-left ...), OR a number (passes through unchanged, so pre-packed positions, deltas and knight moves survive). Also accepts an array/range of values - result lifts element-wise. Text that is not an address or a direction returns a message ""TOPOS: can't read ..."" (text, so it shows in the cell; arithmetic on it gives #VALUE!).¶" &
                "   mult           ¦(Optional) Multiplier for the row component. Default: the _mult constant (1000000), which fits any column up to 999999 (ZZZZ = 475254) and keeps the trailing 6 digits readable as the column. A column >= mult returns a message rather than a wrong number. Applies to both branches: addresses encode as ROW*mult+COLUMN, direction deltas repack as rowDelta*mult+colDelta.¶" &
                "EXAMPLE:       ¦¶" &
                "Formula        ¦=TOPOS(""E5"")¶" &
                "Result         ¦5000005 (and =TOPOS(""↑"") returns -1000000)",
                "¦", "¶"
                ), result)
)
);
